# playtest

Live playtest of the Godot client: the real game with rendering, llm_server (stub turn or the real model), a scripted player, a screenshot per step.

The full procedure is in [.claude/skills/playtest/SKILL.md](mdc:.claude/skills/playtest/SKILL.md).

Read that file when this rule triggers, then follow it.

**Quick reference:**

- gdUnit4 green first, then `python tools/godot_playtest.py` (smoke, stub turn), `--scenario offline`, `--scenario live --real` after prompt changes
- Read `build/playtest/<scenario>/report.txt` and look at every `NN_*.png`
- Crashes: fix + regression test in `game/test/`; other findings: `docs/production/backlog.md`. Never print `.env` keys
